// lexdb over TDS: the seventh bug slice (design/lexdb-robust.md, "The seventh bug slice"), checked against SQL Server 2022 (generated by
// tests/lexdb/gen_mssql.py bugs7 from mssql_bugs7_queries.txt): a SELECT * view keeps its columns as at CREATE VIEW until sp_refreshview
// (by position; 4502 after a column dropped, not caught); 208, 3729, 4502, 4512 and 4513 name objects as the statement wrote them (dbo.T,
// [dbo].[T], the case typed; a view's 208 as its query wrote it), 4512 state 3, 4513 state 2, 102 quoting WITH as typed; DROP INDEX: 159
// for a bare name, 3701 (states 6 and 7) and 3723 (states 4 and 5) naming table.index as written; INFORMATION_SCHEMA.DOMAINS and
// COLUMN_PRIVILEGES; a schema's owner (AUTHORIZATION) in SCHEMATA and sys.schemas. Each batch runs with SET lexdb_batch off and on; each
// expect line: "same: " and the batch's result sets and counts, or its error number.
